  "equipment_type": "Boiler cascade controller via ProtoNode gateway",
  "applies_to": "Hamilton Engineering equipment with the BDB-CDB control, which reports cascade values and up to eight BCB blocks (BCB1-BCB8), connected through a ProtoNode FPC-N54.",
  "summary": "Hamilton Engineering's BDB-CDB control is read over Modbus RTU by a ProtoNode FPC-N54 and served on BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP. The 99-object profile has writable central heating, DHW, indirect DHW, pool and spa setpoints, cascade sensor readings and an anomaly code, then a 9-object block for each of BCB1 to BCB8. This file lists the cascade objects and the BCB1 block.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "50032 (Node_Offset default 50,000 + the BDB-CDB Node-ID 32)",
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Per-boiler blocks repeat every 9 objects: BCB n = the BCB1 instance + 9 x (n - 1), so BCB2 is AI/MI 37-45 and BCB8 is AI/MI 91-99.",
    "The guide only names the device BDB-CDB and does not expand BCB; it does not say which Hamilton products use it.",
    "The table has no read/write column, units or state texts; access is inferred from object type (AV writable, AI/MI read only).",
    "The two anomaly code 2 parts are multistate inputs; their state texts are not given."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Wire the BDB-CDB Modbus port (9600, 8N1) to the ProtoNode R1 port, pick BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP in the Web Configurator, add the BDB-CDB profile with Node-ID 32, and discover the device at 50032. Setpoints are the writable analog values; status and fault information comes from the cascade anomaly and the per-board working status and anomaly codes.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "CH Requests",
        "why": "Central heating request; values not defined in the guide"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 11",
        "name": "Boiler For Heating Setpoint",
        "why": "Boiler setpoint for the heating load"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 12",
        "name": "Dhw SP Temp",
        "why": "Domestic hot water setpoint"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 31",
        "name": "BCB1 Working Status",
        "why": "BCB1 working status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 21",
        "name": "Cascade S1 Temp Sensor Value",
        "why": "Cascade sensor S1 temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 27",
        "name": "Cascade Anomaly",
        "why": "Cascade-level anomaly (fault) code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 32",
        "name": "BCB1 Anom Code 1",
        "why": "BCB1 anomaly code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Device instance = Node_Offset (default 50,000) + Node-ID; the BDB-CDB profile uses Node-ID 32, so 50032 by default.",
      "Modbus side (R1 port): Modbus RTU 9600, 8N1. BMS RS-485 on the R2 port; bias resistors are DIP switches on each port.",
      "Default IP 192.168.1.24 (255.255.255.0); the field protocol is chosen with the Protocol Selector in the Web Configurator.",
      "Each ProtoNode on a subnet needs its own BACnet Network Number (default 50001)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Boiler blocks repeat every 9 instances (BCB n = BCB1 + 9 x (n - 1)); only BCB1 is listed here.",
      "The guide gives no units, ranges or code tables; confirm values with Hamilton Engineering."
    ]
  },
